--- CORRECTION 2026-08-04, recorded rather than smoothed over ---

The divisor above was 1000000 until 2026-08-04 and produced a GATE THAT COULD NOT FAIL. At
scale=12 a 1.0 is 4096, so (v*4096)/1000000 with v in [-1000,1000] gives inputs in [-4,4], i.e.
numerically zero; the diagnostic run p_iotrace measured the reconstructed output as 98,304 EXACT
ZEROS. Such an observable reproduces perfectly across runs, so the determinism check would have
passed on it -- the same defect class SHARK's first gate had (`shark::span` returning mmap zeros)
and the one SIGMA-GPU's patch already documents and corrects with den=1000 / den=28000.

The weights were never affected: FC::_initScale randomizes them at xavier*(1<<scale) ~ 148.

A GATE_NONZERO / GATE_DEGENERATE announcement was added at the same time, so that a degenerate
observable is refused by the harness instead of passing quietly.
